course: dictionary
lesson: 3820
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Read the words around them to find out which meaning the writer wants. The word forgive has three main meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use.
explain: To forgive someone means to stop being angry with them for doing something wrong, and not to punish them. «Aroha forgave a friend for a cruel prank» means Aroha stopped being cross with her friend. Forgave is the past tense of forgive.
explain: Forgiving someone does not mean the wrong thing was all right. Aroha still asked her friend to say sorry to the whole class, because they had all laughed. Forgiving helps both people move on, but you do not have to stay somewhere that is unsafe.
explain: Forgive can also mean to let someone off paying money they owe, as in «I forgive you the money you owe me». And «forgive me» is a polite way to say sorry before you say or ask something. Check the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: Forgive is a verb. Its forms are forgive, forgives, forgave, forgiven and forgiving.
fact: «Forgave» is the past tense of forgive, as in «Aroha forgave a friend».
fact: Forgive means to stop being angry with someone and not try to punish them.
fact: «Forgive me, but ...» is a polite way to say sorry before you say something.
fact: Forgiving someone does not mean that what they did was right.
exercise: «Aroha forgave a friend for a cruel prank.» What does forgave mean here? | Paid her friend the money she owed | Laughed at her friend's prank | *Stopped being angry with her friend and did not punish her | Told the teacher about the prank
exercise: Gran says, «I forgive you the five pounds you owe me.» What does forgive mean here? | Say sorry to you | *Let you off paying the money you owe | Give you a prize for being good | Stop being angry with you
exercise: Mia says, «Forgive me, but can I borrow your pen?» What is "forgive me" doing here? | Giving a reason for the pen | Asking for forgiveness for a crime | *Politely saying sorry before asking something | Telling Mia to be quiet
test: Which of these is the past tense of forgive? | forgiving | *forgave | forgives | forget
test: Does forgiving someone mean the wrong thing was all right? | Only when you feel sad | *No, forgiving does not make the wrong thing right | Only if they are your best friend | Yes, always
exam: Which meaning fits in «Forgive me, but I need to get past.»? | *A polite way to say sorry before asking or saying something | To let someone off a debt | To stop being angry with someone | To punish someone
